# Website typography

Use only these fonts on the storefront. Load via `next/font` CSS variables in `(website)/layout.tsx`.

| Role | Font | CSS token |
|------|------|-----------|
| Body, UI, nav, buttons, product copy, section labels | Inter | `var(--font-inter)` |
| Hero, product titles, category titles | Poppins | `var(--font-poppins)` |
| Premium section headings (FAQ, blog titles, catalog page titles) | Manrope | `var(--font-manrope)` |

```css
/* ✅ GOOD */
body { font-family: var(--font-inter), "Inter", sans-serif; }
.btn, .website-header, .product-copy-content { font-family: var(--font-inter), "Inter", sans-serif; }
.product-detail-title, .category-card-title { font-family: var(--font-poppins), "Poppins", sans-serif; }
.product-section-heading, .store-catalog__title { font-family: var(--font-manrope), "Manrope", sans-serif; }

/* ❌ BAD — do not use */
font-family: "Playfair Display", Georgia, serif;
font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
```

## Rules

- Prefer `var(--font-*)` tokens from `theme.css`; never hardcode Google Font names alone without the CSS variable fallback chain.
- Do not introduce new display/serif fonts for website UI.
- Keep Inter for form fields, accordion questions/answers body, reviews, and buttons.
- Product name / hero / category names → Poppins. Page/section premium headings → Manrope.
